course: dictionary
lesson: 1326
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear many coats. The word call can mean phone someone, shout, give a name, or visit. You work out which meaning is right by reading the words around it. «The sadness after a death is called grief.» Here called means given the name grief, so the sentence is about naming.
explain: «A dad who never calls» means he never phones. The word calls is about the telephone here, not shouting. Ask yourself: what is the sentence about? A phone, a name, a shout, or a visit? That question points you to the meaning.
explain: Call can also be a noun, meaning a phone call, a shout, or a bird's cry. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Call is a verb: call, calls, called, calling.
fact: Call can also be a noun: a call, calls.
fact: To call someone is to phone them, or to shout so they can hear you.
fact: «Called» can mean given a name, as in «is called grief».
fact: Phrases with call include call back, call off (cancel), call out, call on or call in (visit), and call names (insult someone).
exercise: «The sadness after a death is called grief.» What does called mean here? | Shouted loudly | *Given the name | Visited | Phoned
exercise: In «a dad who never calls», what does calls mean? | Shouts at the door | Gives a name | Visits the shops | *Phones his family
exercise: Which meaning of call is a noun? | To phone someone | To give a name | *A phone call, a shout or a bird's cry | To visit someone
test: What does called mean in «Springboks and some gazelles leap high, called pronking or stotting»? | Visited | Phoned | Shouted | *Named, or given the name of
test: Which phrase means cancel? | call on | call in | call back | *call off
exam: Which meaning of call fits «I'll call you after school»? | Give a name | Visit a house | Cry like a bird | *Phone you
